Package: regmorbidity
Type: Package
Title: Extracting Comorbidity from Danish Register Data with Editable Code Lists
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Jie", "Zhang", role = "aut"),
    person("Sara", "Schwartz", email = "saras@clin.au.dk", role = c("aut", "cre")))
Description: A general approach to deriving comorbidity indicators from Danish
    register data. Conditions are defined in plain CSV code lists that users
    edit, extend and version themselves - one file per condition if preferred -
    rather than in code. Medication (ATC) conditions require a configurable
    number of dispensings within a configurable time window, and the onset date
    is the date of the qualifying dispensing. Conditions are extracted one at a
    time and checkpointed to disk, so a long run over the full register resumes
    after an interruption instead of starting over. The code lists distributed
    with the package take their starting point in those used by Prior and
    colleagues (2016) <doi:10.1093/aje/kwv324>; the extraction method here is
    not an implementation of that index and users are expected to revise the
    code lists for their own study.
